# Mobile project

Agent skill: [.cursor/skills/mobile-agent/SKILL.md](../skills/mobile-agent/SKILL.md)

## Scope

`mobile/` — Expo product app. `packages/mobile-ui/` — React Native UI kit. `mobile/modules/sms-sender/` — Android SMS native module.

## Stack

| Concern | Choice |
|---------|--------|
| Framework | Expo (TypeScript, Expo Router), React Native Web |
| Styling | NativeWind; `tailwind.config.js` extends `@webonone/theme` |
| UI | `@webonone/mobile-ui` — not `@webonone/ui-kit` |
| Nav / roles | `@webonone/platform-nav` `buildNavDefsForSessionRole` |
| Auth | Identity login → WebOnOne assumable roles → Identity session-role |

## Env

Config file: `mobile/.env` only (see `mobile/.env.example`). Loaded via `app.config.ts` → `extra` → `mobile/src/shared/config/env.ts`.

| Key pattern | Purpose |
|-------------|---------|
| `*_API_BASE_URL` | Service API bases (include `/api/v1`) |
| `*_ORIGIN` | Peer frontend origins for WebView |
| `GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID` | Android Google Sign-In (optional) |
| `EXPO_NO_METRO_WORKSPACE_ROOT` | Required for Android release in monorepo |

**Local LAN:** use `http://<lan-ip>:port` for physical devices; backends must listen on `0.0.0.0`.

## Auth flow

1. Identity `POST /auth/login` → JWT in `expo-secure-store`.
2. WebOnOne `GET /company/me/assumable-roles` → role selection when needed.
3. Identity `POST /auth/session-role` → reissued JWT.
4. All API calls use `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>` via `mobile/src/shared/services/apiClient.ts`.

## Native vs WebView

| Area | Strategy |
|------|----------|
| Profile, SMS, Email, Payment, Sales, Companies, Settings, Data, Identity/Users, Staff, Calendar, Analytics, Design Forms, Design Website | Native screens |
| Other web-only nav | Browser fallback |

WebView injects JWT into peer `localStorage` + `postMessage` `webonone:platform:init`. Profile is native because Identity web embed stays blank on Android WebView when bootstrapping from injected storage.

## Platform notes

- SMS gateway (This device) is **Android-only**.
- Google Sign-In is Android-only; requires dev/prebuild (not Expo Go).
- Text.lk gateway mode does not require the mobile app.

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w @webonone/mobile-ui
npm run type-check -w @webonone/mobile
```

Manual: `npm run mobile` from repo root; sign in and open a native screen + a WebView peer.
